This file marks a copy of the astro-theme-v7 template that nobody has set up yet.

`pnpm bootstrap` deletes it. Until that runs, a production build stops and explains
why: the copy still carries the original author's identity, so its canonical
URLs, RSS and sitemap would name their domain and the editor would write to
their repository.

    pnpm bootstrap -- --url https://your-domain --repo you/your-repo

The template's own repository builds by setting V7_TEMPLATE_BUILD=1, which is
what CI does. Delete this file yourself only if you are certain the identity in
site.config.json and cms.config.github.json is yours.
